From 2d5433a2596c099d4eefedcf32196da24f4448e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Monivibe <shonhay@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 04:00:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] AutoWoW perf R1+R2: creature terrain refresh throttle,
 cached creature script id

R1 (flagged, default OFF): Map::CreatureRelocation re-ran the full vmap
terrain query (UpdatePositionData -> ProcessTerrainStatusUpdate ->
UpdateMovementFlags) on every spline step (~33.5% + 9.6% + 8.7% in
soak-s2-80-r1). New worldserver.conf keys
AutoWow.Perf.CreatureTerrainRefreshMs / ...Yards (both 0 = legacy,
early-return, refresh every step). When enabled, only mid-spline steps
of AI-driven creatures are throttled; refresh is forced on cell change,
first refresh, phase change, spline end / teleport / non-spline
relocation, falling, vehicle / passenger / transport, and player-
controlled or player-charmed creatures. Players untouched. Pure
predicate in CreatureTerrainRefresh.h with gtest coverage.

R2: Creature::GetScriptId caches the resolved id keyed on
(entry, m_creatureData), so UpdateEntry / script SetEntry / LoadFromDB
re-resolve automatically. Same result as before for every key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
